-- The words a board shows for a zone, a phase or beat, a mode or a colour —
-- `wording.ts`'s refusals, `narration.ts`'s beats and `lighting.ts`'s room
-- colours, gathered as `board-words.ts`'s `BoardWords` (Stage 8, #159).
--
-- Declared rather than hand-written by the owner's decision on #131/#135
-- (20 Sep 2026): DEFINE WORDS is a declaration of its own, not a field of
-- DEFINE GAME. `of:` says which table a word belongs to; the name is the
-- zone, phase/step, mode or colour it is the word for, so `DEFINE WORDS
-- battle` is the words for `DEFINE ZONE battle` and needs no second name.
--
-- Declared, not consumed. `board-words.ts`'s own tables (`WORDING_AREA`,
-- `NARRATION_AREA`, `PHASE`, the mode words, `LEADER_COLOURS`) still stand,
-- unchanged, and `wordsFromRuleset` still only checks a zone/mode/colour
-- exists rather than reading a phrase from here — the wiring that would
-- retire the hand-written tables is Stage 8's own follow-up, deliberately
-- not done in this file (CLAUDE.md: "declare only; do not move any consumer
-- Stage 8 did not already move").
--
-- Left out on purpose, and named rather than silently missing: `wording.ts`'s
-- `VERB` (the verb in "X cannot attack") and `WINDOW` (a timing window's
-- phrase, for a Requirement), and `effects.ts`'s `untilWords` (how long a
-- rule in force lasts, said "your"/"Claude's", singular/plural). All three
-- are viewer-dependent sentence templates with a branch in them, not a flat
-- name -> word lookup, so they do not fit this file's shape. Giving them a
-- home is real design work — either a templated-sentence declaration beside
-- this one, or a further split of DEFINE WORDS — left to a follow-up rather
-- than forced into a table that would lie about what it can say.

-- §3: the twelve areas the manual counts, minus the two effect-language-only
-- routes (`under`, `play`) `zones.rules` also declares — a program needs to
-- name them, but a board never shows them as a place a card sits, so
-- `board-words.ts`'s own tables carry no entry for either and neither does
-- this file. Order follows `zones.rules`.
DEFINE WORDS deck
  of: zone
  you: "your deck"
  text: "the deck"

DEFINE WORDS hand
  of: zone
  you: "your hand"
  text: "hand"

DEFINE WORDS drop
  of: zone
  you: "your Drop Area"
  text: "the Drop"

DEFINE WORDS leader
  of: zone
  you: "the Leader Area"
  text: "the Leader Area"

DEFINE WORDS battle
  of: zone
  you: "your Battle Area"
  text: "the Battle Area"

DEFINE WORDS combo
  of: zone
  you: "your Combo Area"
  text: "the Combo Area"

DEFINE WORDS energy
  of: zone
  you: "your Energy Area"
  text: "the Energy Area"

DEFINE WORDS life
  of: zone
  you: "your Life Area"
  text: "life"

DEFINE WORDS warp
  of: zone
  you: "your Warp"
  text: "the Warp"

DEFINE WORDS unison
  of: zone
  you: "the Unison Area"
  text: "the Unison Area"

DEFINE WORDS zDeck
  of: zone
  you: "your Z-Deck"
  text: "the Z-Deck"

DEFINE WORDS zEnergy
  of: zone
  you: "your Z-Energy Area"
  text: "Z-Energy"

DEFINE WORDS removed
  of: zone
  you: "out of the game"
  text: "out of the game"

-- §6, §7: the six turn phases and the two a turn is not made of (`setup`,
-- `over`), as `narration.ts`'s beat stream names them, plus the five battle
-- sub-flow steps a "phase" beat also narrates (`declared`..`battleEnd`,
-- `board-words.ts`'s own `PHASE_DECLARATION` maps each to `game.rules`'s
-- `mainEnd` or to `battle.rules`'s own step). Order follows `PHASE` there.
DEFINE WORDS charge
  of: phase
  text: "Charge Phase"

DEFINE WORDS main
  of: phase
  text: "Main Phase"

DEFINE WORDS mainEnd
  of: phase
  text: "Main Phase ends"

DEFINE WORDS end
  of: phase
  text: "End Phase"

DEFINE WORDS declared
  of: phase
  text: "Attack declared"

DEFINE WORDS offense
  of: phase
  text: "Offense Step"

DEFINE WORDS defense
  of: phase
  text: "Defense Step"

DEFINE WORDS damage
  of: phase
  text: "Damage Step"

DEFINE WORDS battleEnd
  of: phase
  text: "The battle ends"

DEFINE WORDS setup
  of: phase
  text: "Setting up"

DEFINE WORDS over
  of: phase
  text: "The game is over"

-- §1-10: the only two tokens `zones.rules` declares for a zone's `modes:`.
DEFINE WORDS active
  of: mode
  text: "Active Mode"

DEFINE WORDS rest
  of: mode
  text: "Rest Mode"

-- §1-2-3: the seven colours `attributes.rules`' own `colors` attribute may
-- hold. `room: true` marks the five a Leader can be, and so a room can be lit
-- for (`lighting.ts`'s `LEADER_COLOURS`) — White and Colorless light no room
-- of their own (`colourOf`'s own fallback to Black).
DEFINE WORDS Red
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Red"

DEFINE WORDS Blue
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Blue"

DEFINE WORDS Green
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Green"

DEFINE WORDS Yellow
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Yellow"

DEFINE WORDS Black
  of: color
  room: true
  text: "Black"

DEFINE WORDS White
  of: color
  text: "White"

DEFINE WORDS Colorless
  of: color
  text: "Colorless"
